\newlabel{tab:perfold}{{VII}{7}{Per-fold results. \emph {Train rec.} is the number of records in the training partition; the two folds with fewer than three are the thin folds discussed in the text. \emph {Position-only} is a lookup from a symbol's index within the data word to its most frequent label, against chance levels of $0.500$, $0.750$ and $0.875$. It is a meaningful control only where the withheld word is absent from training; every leave-one-board-out fold reuses the training word, position then determines the label exactly, and the entry is marked \textit {n/a} (Section~\ref {sec:controls})}{table.7}{}}
